  "verbalization": "Isobutyl hexanoate appears to interact with Calmodulin through a series of molecular targets, with WM-115 acting as a central mediator. This interaction is supported by multiple paths, all of which indicate that Isobutyl hexanoate targets WM-115, which in turn is a target of both Volvalerenal E and Br-Xanthone A, all of which ultimately lead to Calmodulin. The consistent evidence suggests that Isobutyl hexanoate may modulate Calmodulin through a pathway involving WM-115, potentially by influencing the activity of its downstream targets. The mechanism is further supported by the presence of multiple distinct targets of WM-115, indicating a complex regulatory network. While the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated, the integrated evidence points to a plausible pathway where Isobutyl hexanoate exerts its effects through WM-115, which then influences Calmodulin via its downstream targets.",
